{"description":"Make eka-steward an official eka-cli plugin (distribution + human entry point) so its commands are invoked as `eka steward ...` with no PATH install. steward implements the plugin contract: `manifest --json` declares contract v1 with a `commands` array registering the `steward` command (args passthrough), and `install` returns a no-op/artifact result. The release assets already follow the `eka-steward-\u003cos\u003e-\u003carch\u003e[.exe]` + SHA256SUMS.txt contract. eka-core adds the official-registry entry (`steward` -\u003e maleolabs/eka-steward) and eka-cli registers the command. Because plugin dispatch inherits the CLI's stdio and imposes no CLI-side deadline (only the manifest/install contract probes are bounded), both one-shot `run` and long-running `serve` dispatch correctly, and the exit code propagates. Installing and answering manifest/version does not require the run/serve commands, but the registered command dispatches the subcommands those work items implement.","acceptanceCriteria":"`eka plugin install steward` installs the checksum-verified binary and `eka steward version` dispatches to `eka-steward version`. | `eka steward \u003cargs\u003e` passes args through to `eka-steward \u003cargs\u003e` with the CLI's stdio inherited and the exit code propagated. | eka-core's OfficialRegistry resolves \"steward\" and eka-cli registers the `steward` command under the official-only + dispatch-time checksum rules. | `eka steward serve` runs as a long-running dispatch with no CLI-side deadline. | docs/release describe the plugin install path and state that no PATH entry is required."}